obs The k5/k6 pair taught the same lesson the prior lap's four RED candidates taught: a chapter-witness's safety depends on whether its asserts read a dated, unchanging testimony file or a living, movable chapter-scope pin. Checking which before claiming saved a wasted build.
obs Network access to the anointed remote (xy) is intermittent in this environment; retrying the fetch/push after a DNS failure succeeded without any state loss, since nothing had yet been pushed.
rota lap 7289, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in. The reading that held: a dated counsel file's exact phrases are concrete, checkable ground that cannot have moved since it was written, while a chapter-status pin is a live value that can and does move -- the distinction that decided which candidate to roster.
